# Normalize line endings to LF for text files at commit time, regardless of each contributor's
# local core.autocrlf setting -- a branch committed with CRLF (see the Wake Forest integration
# branch, 2026-08-14) makes every line look changed even when the real diff is a few dozen lines,
# which makes review effectively impossible. git's own text/binary heuristic decides what counts
# as text; the explicit "binary" overrides below protect files that heuristic could get wrong.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never go through line-ending conversion. Committing the debugging report as a
# PDF made git warn that LF would be replaced by CRLF, which would corrupt the file on checkout.
*.pdf binary
*.h5 binary
*.dll binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.stl binary
*.lut binary
*.pyc binary
*.lib binary
*.vi binary
*.FCStd binary
